# __PACKAGE_NAME_RAW__

__DESCRIPTION_RAW__

This project is a source-linked DeepSeek Harness Tool plugin scaffold generated by `dsh-plugin-dev`. The baseline registers `__TOOL_NAME_RAW__`, validates one string input, and returns a canonical `{ value }` result. Replace that normalization body and its tests with the requested business operation before treating the plugin as complete.

## Development

The project targets DeepSeek Harness `__HARNESS_VERSION_RAW__` at commit `__HARNESS_COMMIT_RAW__`. When the checkout moves, set `DSH_HARNESS_ROOT` before reinstalling dependencies.

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm verify
```

`pnpm verify` checks the pinned source, typechecks, runs the real Tool registry and HMR tests, boots `tests/fixtures/cordis.yml` through the Cordis Loader, builds declarations and JavaScript, and inspects the packed file list.

## Profile installation

After implementing the business behavior and building the package, install the current checkout into a development profile from the project directory:

```sh
dsh plugin --profile demo add .
dsh --profile demo --dump-config
dsh --profile demo
dsh plugin --profile demo remove __PACKAGE_NAME_RAW__
```

The package ships `cordis.patch.yml` as its bundle layer. The stable row id is `__ROW_ID_RAW__`; a later profile patch that replaces this row's `config` must restate every required field.

## Delivery status

The audited DSH runtime dependency closure is not available from the configured npm registry. Development dependencies link to the local pinned Harness checkout, and this package remains `private: true`. Passing local tests proves compatibility with that source snapshot, not independent npm publication readiness.
